# VTID-03791 — commands run this session

## Context: how this VTID was found

While delivering the user's requested "click / visuals / audio" full live
verification of VTID-03779 (Nova session prewarm) on staging, a real
Playwright run against the actual community app (preview-aws.vitanaland.com,
real .vtorb-fab click, real auth) showed `prewarm_ready` observed on every
run, but the WS transcript's `start` send was consistently preceded by a
fresh `connected` — i.e. the cold-connect path, not the reuse branch. Traced
to `GET /live/transport` (orb-live.ts) resolving `isFeatureLive('ORB_WS_TRANSPORT')`
false (unset on staging, code default 'off'), so the widget's real-app tap
used SSE, which never calls `_sessionStartWs()` at all.

## Verification that this flag is real, and confirming the fix works

$ grep -n "FEATURE_ORB_WS_TRANSPORT_ENV" -r vitana-platform
  -> feature-flags.ts has no DEFAULT_SETTINGS entry for ORB_WS_TRANSPORT;
     AWS-STAGE-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml and AWS-PROD-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml both had
     no reference to it before this change -> confirmed default 'off' on
     both stacks, not staging-only as might have been assumed.

Forced the widget's own documented developer override
(`localStorage['vtorb.transport']='ws'`, orb-widget.js) in a real Playwright
session against preview-aws-gateway.vitanaland.com to exercise the reuse
branch ahead of deploying this pin, to confirm the MECHANISM (not just the
config) is correct:

  WS transcript (single tap, forced ws transport):
  {"t":2050.7,"dir":"recv","type":"connected"}
  {"t":2051.1,"dir":"send","type":"prewarm"}
  {"t":2472.1,"dir":"recv","type":"prewarm_ready"}
  {"t":2906.3,"dir":"send","type":"start"}          <- no 'connected' before this
  {"t":4208.2,"dir":"recv","type":"session_started"}
  {"t":4208.9,"dir":"send","type":"audio_ready"}
  {"t":4458.3,"dir":"recv","type":"audio"}
  TAP-TO-FIRST-AUDIO: 1787ms (desktop), 1396ms (mobile)

  Direct cold-vs-warm, same page, back-to-back (forced ws transport):
  WARM (reused prewarmed socket):        1726ms
  COLD (fired immediately after, fresh connect): 1819ms
  Both under the 3s cold-start target.

This confirms pinning FEATURE_ORB_WS_TRANSPORT_ENV=staging-only turns the
above into the DEFAULT behavior for every real staging tap, rather than
something only reachable via a manual localStorage override.

## The change itself

Edited `.github/workflows/AWS-STAGE-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml`: added
`FEATURE_ORB_WS_TRANSPORT_ENV` to both the strip-list and the re-add list
(`value:"staging-only"`) in the task-def jq block, same pattern as every
other pinned flag in this file. No application code touched.

$ python3 -c "import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('.github/workflows/AWS-STAGE-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml'))"
  -> YAML OK

